#  OWNERSHIP RULE (CONTRACT.md §1): tier 1 tracks upstream; everything else is
#  ours.
#
#  Only rts_sources_gcc15's populated directories are excluded, because they are
#  a snapshot of the compiler's own sources that populate.sh reproduces and
#  asserts against both toolchains. Tier 2, tier 3 and every leaf src/ are
#  hand-owned: committed, editable, and never copied over. That is what lets a
#  board file be fixed in place instead of being re-derived, and it retires the
#  prune that three times deleted a correctly-listed hand-authored file.
rts_sources_gcc15/libgnat/
rts_sources_gcc15/libgnarl/
rts_sources_gcc15/libgnat-*/
rts_sources_gcc15/libgnarl-*/
rts_sources_gcc15/librestrictions/

#  ...except the bodies we own inside tier 1. These are the one deliberate
#  exception to "tier 1 tracks upstream": merged variants of units upstream
#  ships twice, carrying an in-body capability test instead of a directory pair
#  (rts_sources_gcc15.gpr, Patched_Dir). They must be re-merged on a GCC bump.
!rts_sources_gcc15/libgnat-patched/
!rts_sources_gcc15/libgnat-patched/*.adb

#  Build output.
*/obj/
*/obj-*/
*/adalib/
*/adalib-*/
*/bin/
*/alire/
*/config/
*.upstream
*.ali
*.o

#  Generated by each leaf's post-fetch/pre-build action from ada_source_path.in,
#  with absolute paths into whichever place Alire put the tier crates -- never
#  commit it (RTS-PRODUCTION.md B1).
*/ada_source_path

#  Alire regenerates gnat_config/ from [configuration.variables] on every build.
#  The hand-written shims live in src/ so generated and authored files are never
#  mixed in one directory (CONTRACT.md §3.3).
*/gnat_config/light_mpfs_config.*
*/gnat_config/light_tasking_mpfs_config.*
*/gnat_config/embedded_mpfs_config.*
*/gnat_config/light_pico_config.*
*/gnat_config/light_tasking_pico_config.*
*/gnat_config/embedded_pico_config.*

#  Written by `make verify`: this host's measured rows (CI uploads it).
metrics.measured
